From 0edb631fb7adc665cf2a123dd7f4d7162bed9540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Merge manager as two processes in swim lanes; liveness
 and stalls; lane order rule

Owner, 2026-11-07: "In the merge manager process need to split into swim
lanes" and "Swap owner lane down to reduce arrows across non interacting
actor lanes... Update bpmn skills".

- merge-request.bpmn (new, Process_MergeRequest): the sibling session's
  side. Is a merge manager active and live? If so, send the six-line
  request; if not, is one needed? Manage its own PRs, or elect one with the
  siblings (the winner announces and takes the lane). A request not
  acknowledged in the stall window goes to stalled-agent triage and a
  re-election without the stalled session.
- merge-manager-watch.bpmn: the merge steward lane, with the owner lane
  below it (next to the only lane it talks to) for the batch card. Split
  by phase so both diagrams pass bpmn:detangle --check with no finding.
- merge-manager-watcher: the sibling's side, where the announcement lives,
  liveness (heartbeat about 10 min) and stalls (about 30 min).
  continual-progress, coordinate, merge-queue: the siblings' side of it.
- bpmn-authoring, bpmn-detangle: lanes sit next to the lanes they exchange
  flows with; no flow crosses a lane it does not stop in.
- roles.json, actors/merge-manager.json: liveness and re-election.
- Regenerated: SVGs, checklists, .pot files, the sdlc/processes README rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
