+msgid "The elected session holds the merge steward lane and runs its loop until it hands over or the lane lapses."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:48
+#. Diagram element documentation
+msgid "The measured condition (laneNeeded): two or more active sessions have ready PRs in the same repositories, and either the runners are contended (more than about 10 queued runs on a repository, or the oldest queued run older than about 30 minutes) or PRs conflict with or supersede each other (owner ruling, 2026-11-07)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:98
+#. Diagram element documentation
+msgid "The merge manager owns the landing from here: it reports landed, or hands the PR back with the reason."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:16
+#. Diagram element documentation
+msgid "The sibling's side of merging (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). A coding agent with a PR ready to merge does not know whether a merge manager exists, so it checks: if one is active and live, it sends the six-line merge request; if none is, it measures whether one is needed, and either runs the merge manager loop for its own PRs or elects one with its siblings by the fixed rule, the winner announcing itself to all and taking the lane. Any agent may stall, the merge manager included: a request not acknowledged within the stall window sends the sibling to stalled-agent triage and a re-election without the stalled session. The merge manager's own loop is Process_MergeManagerWatch."
